index 0000000..02a9251
--- /dev/null
+++ b/QUIET_sims_v32/results/MANIFEST.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Result files: what made them and with which parameters
+
+Every run file written since Task 13 starts with a `meta` block (`scripts/meta.js`): the script and its arguments, the time,
+the git commit before the run, the engine file and its SHA-1, and `params` with the full physical and numerical set-up
+(wavelength, n_eff, Γ, R, loss, ε, cell geometry, inclusions, dithers, beamlet lattice, layouts, definitions of the output
+keys). Older files carry their parameters in the top-level keys and in REPORT.md; the table lists where.
+
+| task | REPORT | script(s) | result files | parameters in the file |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 9 / 9b input dither, beamlet model | 6c, 6d | `scripts/t9_input_states.js` | `results/t9*/*.json` | band, R, dBcm, sigma, lattice, `conf` (waist, angle, position, samples), `dlams`; cell = `scripts/cells.js` defaults (4 mm, 16 × 50 µm) |
+| 10 design levers | 6e | `scripts/t10_design.js` | `results/t10/*.json` | top-level keys; variants in `table.md` |
+| 11 grating design 5–20 mm | 6f | `scripts/t11_sizes.js`, `t11_analysis.py` | `results/t11/final_*.json`, `artifact_data.json`, `summary.json` | band, R, dBcm, `c_cal`, `dlams`, `design`, `dithers`, `cells[*].cell` (n_inc, inc_r, out_facet, r); XMAX 250 µm |
+| 12 100 ms limits | 6g | `scripts/t12_fast.py` | `results/t12/fast.json`, `table.md` | the script docstring (drift, referencing, detector, power) |
+| 13 wave vs ray | 6h | `scripts/t13_wave_vs_ray.js` | `results/t13/*.json`, `table.md` | `meta` (added after the run from the script constants) |
+| 14 waists, membrane modulation | 6i | `scripts/t14_waist_mod.js`, `t14_analysis.py`, `t14_compact.py`, `t14_outlook.py`, `t14_artifact_data.py` | `results/t14/*_R*.json`, `artifact_data.json`, `summary.json`, `compact.json`, `outlook.json`, `table.md` | `meta` in every run file; `artifact_data.json` carries the four run `meta` blocks |
+
+Figures. `scripts/build_t14_artifacts.py` puts Task 14 into the published Fig. 2 and Fig. 3 pages
+(`artifacts/fig2_src_t14.html`, `artifacts/fig3_src_t14.html` → `artifacts/fig2_v32.html`, `artifacts/fig3_v32.html`). Both
+default to the same design and parameters (10 mm cell, 3.3 µm, R 97 %, grating-coupler input, ±81 pm, membrane δn_eff 1e-4,
+synchronous averaging, ε 1e-6, 30 layouts); every data set in the pages carries `desc` and, for Task 14, `params` with the
+run provenance, and the pages' "Download settings" files include them.
